<title>USA: Record price paid for CBOT commodity options seat.</title>
<headline>Record price paid for CBOT commodity options seat.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Commodity Options Membership (COM) on the Chicago Board of Trade sold for a record $151,000 Tuesday, the CBOT said.</p>
<p>The previous record was $150,000 on April 25, 1996.</p>
<p>Current bid and offer for a COM membership are $145,000 and $157,000, respectively.</p>
<p>The COM membership allows trading of all CBOT options contracts.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
